# tests/test_log_price.bd - T18: WHAT DOES log() ACTUALLY COST?
#
# ONE QUESTION: does log() cost exactly one tick no matter what you hand it,
# or does the price scale with the STRING'S LENGTH, with the NUMBER OF
# CONCATENATION OPERATIONS used to build the argument, or with the optional
# second Color argument?
#
# WHY THIS ONE IS LOAD-BEARING
#   Every trace this investigation owns was produced by lines of this shape:
#     log("DEBUG TIME: " + label + ", +" + str(get_unix_time() - t0) + "s")
#   and every one of them has been budgeted at ONE tick, because
#   field_notes.txt's CPU LOAD section says "Every line a script runs costs
#   1 tick ... Plain statements - assignments, if/loop bodies, log() calls -
#   all count." One tick. Per line.
#   But the v1.1.0 changelog (Official documentation/Updates/v1.1.0 -
#   Persistence.txt, line 60) says something that cannot be true of a
#   per-LINE accountant: "Fixed scripts being able to dodge CPU-tick cost
#   just by writing an expression in a particular order - the same function
#   call, wrapped in identical arithmetic, could cost wildly different
#   amounts of tick budget depending only on which side of the expression it
#   sat on - costs the same either way now." An accountant that could be
#   fooled by which SIDE of an expression a call sat on is an accountant that
#   WALKS THE EXPRESSION TREE. If it still does, that debug line is not one
#   tick - it is four concatenations, one subtraction, str(), get_unix_time()
#   and five leaf reads, i.e. somewhere around 7-12 ticks, 6-12x what it was
#   budgeted at. Every instrumented number in field_notes would then be
#   inflated, all in the same direction, by the instrument itself.
#   That is the whole reason this test exists: to find out whether this
#   project's own measuring stick is honest before T19-T25 print timings
#   that everyone is expected to believe.
#
# THE UNIT IS DELIBERATELY THE SAME AS T05's: six measured source lines
#   inside a timed bracket, so any delta converts identically in both tests
#   (delta / 6 = per-line cost in seconds; divide by T02's seconds-per-tick
#   to get ticks). At base tier, 0.1s per line = exactly 1 extra tick.
#
# THE SEVEN ARMS - every arm is the same function with the same line count,
# the same loop, the same sleeps and the same bracket. ONLY the six measured
# lines differ, and between the key pairs they differ in exactly one way:
#
#   NOLOG   b = 1                          control: a bare line, nothing printed
#   SHORT   log(s1)                        s1 = "zz"        (2 chars)
#   LONG    log(big)                       big = ~241 chars (120x longer)
#   COLOR   log(s1, Color.amber)           SHORT + one extra argument
#   CONCAT  log(p1 + p2 + p3 + p4)         3 concat ops, 4 reads, ZERO calls
#   SHORTB  log(s1)                        SHORT again - drift/scrollback control
#   DBUG    log(p1 + lbl + p2 + str(get_unix_time() - t0) + p3)
#                                          the real production instrumentation
#                                          line: 4 ops, 1 sub, 2 calls, 5 reads
#
#   LONG vs SHORT and COLOR vs SHORT are PERFECTLY matched pairs - identical
#   expression trees, identical node counts, differing in exactly one thing
#   (character count / one extra argument). Those two comparisons are clean
#   in a way nothing else in this programme is.
#
# HOW TO READ THE RESULT - every delta is against THIS SAME RUN's arms,
# never against another run. Five identical runs in this investigation died
# at +40.7/+111.0/+40.3/+65.5/+64.3s; cross-run comparison of absolute
# timings is not a thing this corpus has earned the right to do.
#
#   STRICT PER-LINE CHARGING (the docs are right; our instrumentation is
#   honest and cheap):
#     ALL SEVEN arm means agree within T03's noise floor (about +/-0.10s per
#     round), including DBUG. d_concat and d_dbug are both under 0.15s.
#     -> log() is one tick, full stop. Argument complexity is free. Every
#        "DEBUG TIME" line in every trace cost what it was budgeted. Close
#        the "log() distorts its own trace" worry permanently.
#
#   PER-OPERATION (or per-node) CHARGING - the changelog was describing live
#   behaviour and the tree-walk is still there:
#     d_concat >= 1.5s per round  (6 lines x ~3 extra nodes x 0.1s = ~1.8s)
#     AND d_dbug >= 3.5s per round (6 lines x ~7 extra nodes = ~4.2s)
#     -> the ubiquitous debug line costs 7-12 ticks, not 1. Every
#        instrumented span in field_notes is inflated by roughly one tick per
#        operator in every checkpoint line, and the per-token/per-item traces
#        (which log twice per item) need re-reading with that correction
#        before any of their "this call costs 14.3s" numbers are quoted again.
#
#   LENGTH COSTS (per-character work in the printer):
#     d_long >= 0.4s per round, or LONG is killed while SHORT survived.
#     -> print_dashboard()'s long formatted rows are a real unbudgeted cost
#        and every wide banner/table line in menu.bd is more expensive than a
#        short one. At ~241 chars vs 2, d_long/6/239 is the per-character
#        price; multiply by a typical 70-char dashboard row for the real bill.
#     LENGTH IS FREE: d_long within +/-0.15s of zero -> formatting width is
#        not a lever; stop worrying about it.
#
#   COLOUR COSTS:
#     d_color ~= +0.6s per round (6 lines x 1 tick) -> the second argument is
#        charged as its own node; log(msg, Color.x) is 2 ticks, not 1.
#     d_color ~= 0 -> colour is free; use it freely for readability.
#
#   DRIFT / SCROLLBACK CONFOUND (this is why SHORTB exists):
#     SHORTB is the SAME arm as SHORT, run five arms later, after ~96 payload
#     lines have been printed - including 24 very long ones. If
#     |shortb - short| < 0.15s, there is no scrollback cost and no session
#     warm-up, and the ascending arm order is safe.
#     IF |shortb - short| >= 0.3s, THE ARM ORDER IS CONFOUNDED: the later
#     arms are the expensive-looking ones by construction, so d_concat and
#     d_dbug are NOT trustworthy from this run. Report it and re-run with the
#     arm order reversed before believing any per-operation conclusion.
#     This is also the only per-line evidence about terminal-buffer growth
#     anyone in this programme has collected.
#
#   INVALID RUN: if NOLOG is not the smallest mean, something drifted;
#     report it and re-run. No delta from that run means anything.
#
#   INTEGER CLOCK: if every burst= prints as a whole number (0, 1, 2...),
#     get_unix_time() has 1-second resolution and burst= is unusable. In that
#     case use each arm's SPAN instead: subtract its ARM-START at= from its
#     ARM-DONE at=. Every arm's sleeps and boundary lines are identical, so
#     span differences are exactly 4x the mean differences above - the same
#     effects, four times larger, and they survive 1-second quantization.
#
#   WHAT COUNTS AS A "NODE" is itself unknown, so two figures are printed.
#     If variable READS are free and only operators/calls are charged, DBUG
#     has 7 chargeable nodes more than SHORT (4 concats + 1 subtraction +
#     str() + get_unix_time()) and CONCAT has 3. If reads are charged too,
#     those become 11 and 6. SUM4's per_op and SUM8's per_node both assume
#     the reads-are-free reading; halve them for the other. The two figures
#     only differ in the constant, never in the verdict.
#
# IS THE BURST THE EXPERIMENT? YES - deliberately, and this is the one place
#   the ~10-line unpaced-burst rule is knowingly approached.
#   Six unpaced log() lines is the payload being priced; it cannot be paced
#   without destroying the measurement. Sizing: under per-line charging every
#   arm is 6 ticks = 0.6s of load, trivially safe. Under per-node charging
#   the worst arm, DBUG, is ~12 ticks x 6 = ~72 ticks... which at base tier
#   is ~7s of continuous 100% and WILL trip the 5-second kill.
#   THAT IS NOT A FAILURE. THAT IS THE RESULT, IN THE HARDER CURRENCY:
#   if DBUG dies while SHORT ran four clean rounds, per-operation charging is
#   confirmed outright and the exact production debug line is proven lethal
#   six-in-a-row. Everything is ordered so that death costs nothing else:
#     - arms ascend in predicted cost, so the cheap clean pairs bank first;
#     - SHORTB (the validity control) runs BEFORE DBUG, not after;
#     - the ENTIRE summary for arms 1-6 is printed BEFORE DBUG starts.
#   A run that dies inside DBUG still delivers six arms fully analysed.
#   Known-lethal reference points: ~13 unpaced log() calls in a tight loop
#   (field notes) and 50 unpaced arithmetic lines (test_cpu_decay.bd). Six is
#   comfortably under both unless argument complexity is charged - which is
#   exactly the hypothesis.
#
# ZERO get_cpu() CALLS. get_cpu()'s own cost is itself unresolved (that is
#   T05's job) and field_notes carries a player CORRECTION saying it adds
#   load despite the docs. Importing an unquantified perturbation into the
#   one test whose subject is measurement honesty would be self-defeating.
#   Wall clock only. The price paid: this script cannot verify that every arm
#   started from the same meter state. SHORTB is the substitute for that
#   check - an empirical one that needs no instrument.
#
# HOW TO RUN
#   1) Run T02 (test_tick_ruler) first and have its seconds-per-tick to hand;
#      this test reports seconds, and only T02 converts them into ticks.
#      T02 must have CONFIRMED that the engine blocks on tick exhaustion -
#      if it REFUTED that, wall-clock deltas measure nothing and this whole
#      script must be re-cut to kill / no-kill observables.
#   2) Fresh session if convenient. Run `ps` and `jobs`, confirm nothing else
#      is running, and paste that output too.
#   3) Save as ~/scripts/test_log_price.bd and run `test_log_price`.
#      No parameters. One execution. ~3 minutes.
#   4) PASTE BACK: every line that does NOT begin with a lowercase z.
#      Every payload/filler line printed inside a timed bracket begins with
#      "z" and carries no information - it IS the thing being measured, not a
#      result. Every line worth pasting begins with LOGPRICE, PRECHECK, ARM-,
#      R or SUM.
#   5) ONE EXCEPTION: also paste the FIRST "z0123456789..." line you see, in
#      full, exactly once. That is the LONG arm's payload and pasting one
#      proves the terminal actually rendered all ~241 characters (it must end
#      in ...0123456789). If it is truncated, d_long measures truncation, not
#      length, and the LENGTH verdict is void.
#   6) REPEATS: TWO runs, back to back, same session. A third only if
#      d_concat or d_dbug lands on opposite sides of the 0.15s / 1.5s
#      decision band between the two runs, or if SHORTB disagrees with SHORT
#      in one run but not the other.
#   7) If it dies: paste everything that printed anyway. The last ARM-START
#      line names the arm that killed it and the last R line names the round,
#      which is a complete result on its own.
#
# IF IT DIES WITH ZERO OUTPUT: this file is ~420 lines, most of it this
#   header, and nobody has ever established whether comment lines and func
#   declarations cost ticks at load time (T09/test_cpu_ceiling.bd is the test
#   that settles it). The sleep(1) between every func definition below exists
#   to absorb that. If it still prints nothing at all, that is a T09 result,
#   not a T18 one - strip this header down to its first ten lines and re-run;
#   if the stripped copy runs, file length costs ticks at load and every long
#   script in this project starts from a hole.

var t0 = get_unix_time()
var SML = "zz"
var BIG = "z012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789"
var P1 = "zz "
var P2 = " +"
var P3 = "s"
var P4 = "cc"
var LBL = "DBG"

sleep(1)

func arm_nolog(tz):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var b = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        b = 1
        b = 1
        b = 1
        b = 1
        b = 1
        b = 1
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=NOLOG burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_short(tz, s1):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=SHORT burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_long(tz, s1):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=LONG burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_color(tz, s1):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        log(s1, Color.amber)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=COLOR burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_concat(tz, a1, a2, a3, a4):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        log(a1 + a2 + a3 + a4)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=CONCAT burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_shortb(tz, s1):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        log(s1)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=SHORTB burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

func arm_dbug(tz, a1, a2, a3, lb):
    var s = 0
    var r = 0
    var ts = 0
    var el = 0
    while r < 4:
        sleep(1)
        ts = get_unix_time()
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        log(a1 + lb + a2 + str(get_unix_time() - tz) + a3)
        el = get_unix_time() - ts
        sleep(2)
        s = s + el
        r = r + 1
        log("R" + str(r) + " arm=DBUG burst=" + str(el) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - tz))
    return s / 4

sleep(1)

# --- preflight: prove Color.amber resolves before an entire arm depends on
# --- it. If this raises, the COLOR arm is void but every other arm is fine.

log("LOGPRICE start arms=7 rounds=4 lines=6 clock=" + str(t0))
sleep(1)
try:
    log("PRECHECK color ok", Color.amber)
catch e:
    log("PRECHECK color FAILED - COLOR arm is void: " + e.message)
sleep(1)
log("LOGPRICE note - paste every line NOT starting with z, plus ONE full z0123... payload line")

# --- driver: arms ascend in predicted cost. SHORTB (validity control) and
# --- the whole summary for arms 1-6 run BEFORE the riskiest arm, DBUG.

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=NOLOG payload='b = 1' at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mNOLOG = arm_nolog(t0)
log("ARM-DONE arm=NOLOG mean=" + str(mNOLOG) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=SHORT payload='log(2-char)' at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mSHORT = arm_short(t0, SML)
log("ARM-DONE arm=SHORT mean=" + str(mSHORT) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=LONG payload='log(241-char)' at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mLONG = arm_long(t0, BIG)
log("ARM-DONE arm=LONG mean=" + str(mLONG) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=COLOR payload='log(2-char, Color.amber)' at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mCOLOR = arm_color(t0, SML)
log("ARM-DONE arm=COLOR mean=" + str(mCOLOR) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=CONCAT payload='log(a+b+c+d)' 3ops 0calls at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mCONCAT = arm_concat(t0, P1, P4, P2, P3)
log("ARM-DONE arm=CONCAT mean=" + str(mCONCAT) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=SHORTB payload='log(2-char)' DRIFT CONTROL at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mSHORTB = arm_shortb(t0, SML)
log("ARM-DONE arm=SHORTB mean=" + str(mSHORTB) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

# --- INTERIM SUMMARY: everything except DBUG, printed before DBUG can kill
# --- the run. Paced one line per sleep so a kill here loses at most one line.

sleep(2)
log("SUM1 nolog=" + str(mNOLOG) + " short=" + str(mSHORT) + " d_short=" + str(mSHORT - mNOLOG) + " per_line=" + str((mSHORT - mNOLOG) / 6))
sleep(1)
log("SUM2 LENGTH long=" + str(mLONG) + " d_long=" + str(mLONG - mSHORT) + " per_line=" + str((mLONG - mSHORT) / 6) + " (>=0.4 => per-character work)")
sleep(1)
log("SUM3 COLOUR color=" + str(mCOLOR) + " d_color=" + str(mCOLOR - mSHORT) + " per_line=" + str((mCOLOR - mSHORT) / 6) + " (~0.6 => colour is its own tick)")
sleep(1)
log("SUM4 CONCAT concat=" + str(mCONCAT) + " d_concat=" + str(mCONCAT - mSHORT) + " per_line=" + str((mCONCAT - mSHORT) / 6) + " per_op=" + str((mCONCAT - mSHORT) / 18))
sleep(1)
log("SUM5 DRIFT shortb=" + str(mSHORTB) + " drift=" + str(mSHORTB - mSHORT) + " (>=0.3 => arm order CONFOUNDED, distrust SUM2/SUM4/SUM7)")
sleep(1)
log("SUM6 arms 1-6 banked - starting DBUG, the only arm that may be lethal")

# --- riskiest arm last: the literal production instrumentation line.

sleep(2)
log("ARM-START arm=DBUG payload='log(p+lbl+p+str(get_unix_time()-t0)+p)' at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))
var mDBUG = arm_dbug(t0, P1, P2, P3, LBL)
log("ARM-DONE arm=DBUG mean=" + str(mDBUG) + " at=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0))

sleep(2)
log("SUM7 DEBUGLINE dbug=" + str(mDBUG) + " d_dbug=" + str(mDBUG - mSHORT) + " per_line=" + str((mDBUG - mSHORT) / 6))
sleep(1)
log("SUM8 per_node=" + str((mDBUG - mSHORT) / 42) + " (7 chargeable nodes x 6 lines, reads assumed free; halve if reads are charged - compare to SUM4 per_op)")
sleep(1)
log("SUM9 VERDICT all d within 0.15 => PER-LINE, instrumentation honest; d_concat>=1.5 and d_dbug>=3.5 => PER-OPERATION, every trace inflated")
sleep(1)
log("LOGPRICE DONE 7/7 arms x 4 rounds total=+" + str(get_unix_time() - t0) + "s - paste every non-z line")
